BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-23-str1-strength-lower-body-@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261123T183000
DTEND:20261123T190500
SUMMARY:[RW] Strength: lower-body strength (single-leg strength) (35 min)
DESCRIPTION:Runner\, 5 km to half marathon: better running economy and rac
 e pace. Lift with 2-3 reps in reserve\, stop a set if form breaks. Streng
 th starts at least 3 hours after cardio (practice).\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not
  medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-pl
 an
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-24-run1-easy-run-with-stride@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261124T063000
DTEND:20261124T070000
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy run with strides (30 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 7 min easy\; 6 x (0.33 min hard + 1 min easy)
 \; 5 min cool-down. Six relaxed fast strides of about 20 s (RPE 7\, smoot
 h\, not a sprint) with easy jogging between. Easy means RPE 2-3: you can 
 talk in full sentences. Use your watch's easy heart-rate zone if you have
  one.\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you mo
 ve means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
